- RELAYED, **the mechanism the gate measured (`c3-shift-mechanism.md`, 968 of 968 pill states)**: the pill's parent is the content column `div.flex.min-h-full.min-w-0.flex-1.flex-col.self-stretch` (`AppShell.tsx` line 166 at main; `<FeedbackButton />` at line 184 is its last child and the pill is `position: fixed`, so it takes no room); the column's child `main` is `flex-1`. A padding P at the column's end therefore adds to the column's content height; the column's box is `max(S, C + P)` (S is the height its row gives it, C its content); `main` gives up its spare room (S - C) first. So document growth **g = max(0, C + P - S) - max(0, C - S)**, which lies in [0, P]; `main` shrinks by **D = min(S - C, P)** when there is spare room; and **g + D = P exactly**. The gate printed: "growth of the document + what the column's flex-1 child gave up = 96" in 968 of 968 states. **That identity is the property every geometry row of this kit is built on.**
