## STANDING LINES
1. **PRIOR-WORK CHECK, before you edit.** In your clone: `git log --oneline -n 8 1873d0c -- web/src/components/customer/CustomerManagement.tsx web/src/components/feedback/FeedbackPill.module.css web/src/components/feedback/FeedbackPill.room.test.tsx web/src/components/partner/OneCustomerEstimate.name.test.tsx`; `git log -S'data-row-menu' --oneline 1873d0c -- web` (expected: nothing; positive control `-S'data-scroll-x'` at least 1); `git log -S':has(> .pill)' --oneline 1873d0c -- web` (expected: exactly the branch's room commit). Read as claims: the gate's `2026-11-02_B1079_STATUS.md` whole and its evidence files named above; the previous builder's `Briefs/2026-11-01_B1073_STATUS.md` (its Corrections 1 and 5: the menu is opened by keyboard because a click scrolls and closes it; the room rule is screen-only); `Briefs/2026-10-30_B959_STATUS.md` (the list pages and the pill's first sighting). **Prior work is NOT redone and NOT undone:** the pill's place, size, colour and text; the footer room rule; the declined cells c1 and c2 (still declined; the pill covers a row's Actions button at scroll 0 until the page is scrolled about 40 px); the lists restyle; item A; item 2 of the 409 ticket stays "measured only". **A READY FOR QA without a PRIOR WORK section is returned unread.**
2. **PHASE SCOPE.** As the fourth paragraph. Nothing in this lane connects to a device, fleet, firmware, SIEM or Security Manager tool.
3. **No production, no demo or UAT deploy, no hosted site, no HTTP to any hosted host, no `az`, no Kudu, no docker, no ssh session.** Network: `npm ci` (the registry), the one `git fetch` and the one `git push`, `gh` (`-X GET`) only. Browser measures talk to `127.0.0.1` ports in your block only.
4. **No message to any human.** No mail, chat or PR comment; you never open, merge, edit or comment on a PR and never write Jira (reads only, every JQL `project = HPSMPOC AND ( ... )`). No person's name in STATUS, code, test names or messages (say "the product owner"). No decision-card id, `C-` entry number, ticket key or `B###` in changed lines or messages. No Artifact, Docs, publish, decision-queue or scoreboard tool.
5. **WORDS.** No customer-visible string changes and no new accessible text. The only product byte you add is one `data-*` attribute. Prove it by M4, A1, and the page-text and accessibility-tree equality of step 11 (i).
6. **Never skip a failure.** Fix the root cause and re-verify end to end; never `.skip`, retry-to-green, sleep-for-timing or environment-gate a row. **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -d/-D`, `--prune`, `update-ref -d`, `worktree prune`, `gc`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`, `checkout -- <file>`, `sed -i`); quarantine to `.tools/b1090/_quarantine/` (the scratch spec goes there at the end of each run). A planted file is restored by `cp` from the committed blob. The one removal allowed is your own `heavy.lock` (removed by the lock helper).
7. **Shell:** never type `cd` (a hook refuses it); absolute single-quoted paths (they contain `!`); `git -C`; `git --no-optional-locks` for read verbs; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; `${VAR}:path` (zsh reads `$H:w...` as a modifier); heredocs QUOTED; `bash` for arrays and `PIPESTATUS`; python only as `python3 -I -B`; no unquoted word starting with `=`; no `rm`, no `sed -i`. **Every count printed in STATUS is printed by the command that makes it.** Stop every process you start; kill only by pid plus cwd. Every closed list in this kit is stated as a property first: "at least these" never means "only these".
8. **Locks and heartbeats.** `lock.sh` wraps git REF WRITES and the fetch/push on the shared `.tools/.git-lock` (exits 99 after 10 minutes: write its mtime into STATUS and end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <is .tools/.git-lock stale>`). Heavy jobs (`npm ci`, build, every `vitest` and `playwright` run, the plants) take the seat-local `.tools/b1090/heavy.lock`, one at a time, only while load1 is below 7 on two reads about 4 s apart. Every waiter prints a heartbeat figure that MOVES at least every 30 s into `.tools/b1090/logs/heartbeat.txt`; frozen for 3 beats = stuck: say so.
